  "text": "The most important decision was treating the rules as part of the interface. Most of what makes Betsy feel fair is invisible: hidden odds, refunds when both miss, a payout that can only happen once. A wireframe cannot show a race between two phones. Designing the screens and the database rules side by side surfaced product problems no static screen could have shown. What I do not know yet: whether virtual points keep a group playing past the first weeks, and whether every one of these mechanics belongs in a game about friends.",
